00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.710 align:start position:0%
minister leonel carmen says pop-up  clinics last summer helped the province  cut the number of people who were  unvaccinated in half currently 92  percent of quebec adults have received  at least one shot of the vaccine but  that still leaves over 500 thousand  quebecers who have not yet received  their first dose camas says the  unvaccinated are really three separate  groups anti-vaccine the vaccine hesitant  and marginalized populations he says the  government is partnering with community  organizations in order to target the  last two groups there's a new phone line  for people who want to discuss the risks  and benefits of vaccination with a  professional and there will be more  pop-up clinics that take walk-ins  beginning with one this thursday at the  clsc san catherine in downtown montreal  but the minister was also asked why the  government wasn't going even further  like knocking on doors or even  attempting to call people directly who  haven't been vaccinated he said that is  not his approach all these little things  that we want to do  will give us as many people as possible  that we can reach i mean i'm sure  i'm not thinking i'm going to reach 100  of the population but i want to reach as  many as possible to make this as  effective as possible the question now  though is if not one hundred percent how  many people can the government reach  camach said he would not set a specific  target for himself  raquel fletcher global news quebec city
 

